# EMDR — redpen for copy

Whenever you **write, rewrite, critique, or polish user-facing text**, use the **redpen** skill first (`~/.agents/skills/redpen/SKILL.md` or invoke `/redpen`).

## When this applies

- Marketing / landing / about / pricing (see **marketing-no-explain-copy** — no explanatory body paragraphs)
- Onboarding, auth, billing, upgrade modals, empty states
- Buttons, labels, errors, help, emails, in-app microcopy
- Admin copy that end users might see

## Do

1. Load and follow **redpen** (truth ledger → reader moment → territories → preference loop → finishing gates).
2. Still obey **nura-brand** (Nura, no BLS jargon, pistachio voice, sentence case, **no em dash `—`** in user-facing sentences).
3. Ship finished copy into the product files — do not leave only a chat draft when the task is to change UI.

## Page / screen changes

After creating or editing a **page or UI surface**, also run the full end review in `.cursor/rules/page-copy-design-review.mdc` (**redpen** + **writing-copy** + **frontend-design**). If anything fails, propose and apply fixes in the same turn.

## Do not

- Draft marketing or UI copy from generic SaaS templates without redpen
- Echo the same phrase in kicker + title + lead + CTA
- Invent metrics, testimonials, or clinical claims

Skip redpen only for pure code/config comments, commit messages, or changelog bullets that are not user-facing.
